<!-- PAGE 4: BERLIN & PRAGUE — THE SIBERIAN BLUEPRINT        -->
<!-- ======================================================= -->
<div class="page">

  <div class="slugline">INT. VILLA SCHLACHTENSEE - MUSIC ROOM - EVENING (1938)</div>
  <p class="action">Berlin. A warm fire glows. Reinhard and ERIKA CANARIS (wife of the Abwehr Chief) play a Bach double-violin concerto. Their instruments harmonize with razor precision.</p>
  <p class="action">On the sofa, ADMIRAL WILHELM CANARIS sips Mosel wine beside Lina, nodding to the tempo.</p>
  <p class="action">The music concludes on a sharp, sustained chord. Polite applause.</p>

  <div class="character">CANARIS</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(wry smile)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">If only the Abwehr and the SD were as finely tuned as those two violins, Reinhard.</div>

  <div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(lowering his bow, unsmiling)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">Harmony requires discipline, Herr Admiral. When one instrument plays out of turn, it must be retuned. Or replaced.</div>

  <div class="slugline">INT. CASTLE JUNGFERN-BRESCHAN - STUDY - NIGHT (JANUARY 1942)</div>
  <p class="action">Prague. A massive map of the Russian continent unrolled across an oak desk. Heydrich uses a red pencil to circle massive swathes of the Ural Mountains and Siberia.</p>
  <p class="action">Lina enters carrying a tray with hot tea.</p>

  <div class="character">LINA</div>
  <div class="dialogue">You are barely home and you bury yourself in papers. What is this conference in Wannsee you have summoned everyone to?</div>

  <div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(tracing the Ural line with his pencil)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">The final solution to the European Jewish question. We are organizing the complete transfer to the East.</div>

  <div class="character">LINA</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(frowning, setting down the tray)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">To Siberia? Millions of people? Reinhard... how could they survive in those barrens?</div>

  <div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(voice calm, clinical, detached)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">Siberia has coal, ore, timber. The strong will build the roads. Naturally, a great percentage will fall away through natural attrition. The rest will work. It is an immense engineering problem, Lina. Nothing more.</div>

</div>

