<!-- PAGE 5: PRAGUE — HOLEŠOVICE CURVE (MAY 27, 1942)       -->
<!-- ======================================================= -->
<div class="page">

  <div class="slugline">EXT. PRAGUE-HOLEŠOVICE - TRAM LOOP CURVE - 10:35 AM</div>
  <p class="action">A hairpin bend beneath suburban villas. A streetcar groans along the tracks.</p>
  <p class="action">JAN KUBIŠ leans against the railing, his hand inside his raincoat clutching an altered anti-tank grenade. On the opposite corner stands JOSEF GABČÍK, trench coat draped over his folded STEN submachine gun.</p>
  <p class="action">Around the crest of the hill, a pocket mirror FLASHES twice: signal from Valčík.</p>
  <p class="action">The green open Mercedes descends the slope. Klein slows the heavy car to navigate the tight turn.</p>
  <p class="action">Gabčík steps into the street. Directly in front of the radiator. He whips the Sten gun to his shoulder, stares directly at Heydrich, and pulls the trigger.</p>
  <p class="action">CLICK. A misfire. The bolt jams.</p>

  <div class="character">KLEIN</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(shouting, stomping the brakes)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">Herr Obergruppenführer!</div>

  <p class="action">Instead of ducking or ordering Klein to floor the gas, Heydrich RISES to his feet inside the car. His face is pale with fury. He unholsters his 7.65mm pistol and aims point-blank at Gabčík.</p>

  <div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
  <div class="dialogue">Shoot the dog!</div>

  <p class="action">Behind the bumper, Kubiš steps forward with a bowler-shaped bomb. He hurls it with an underhand swing.</p>
  <p class="action">KABOOM! The blast lifts the rear wheel off the asphalt. Black smoke, shattered metal, horsehair upholstery, and dirty road dust erupt into the air.</p>
  <p class="action">Heydrich staggers out through the passenger door, pistol smoking, firing blindly into the fumes—before collapsing face-down against the warm radiator grille.</p>

  <div class="slugline">INT. BULOVKA HOSPITAL - WARD - NIGHT (JUNE 3, 1942)</div>
  <p class="action">Lina sits beside the high iron hospital bed. Reinhard’s face is sunken, bathed in feverish sweat. The wound from the grenade splinter has turned septic.</p>

  <div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(barely a breath)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">Lina... go back to Fehmarn. Take the children home.</div>

  <div class="character">LINA</div>
  <div class="dialogue">Hush. You will come home with us.</div>

  <p class="action">His eyes roll toward the ceiling. His dry lips move:</p>

  <div class="character">HEYDRICH</div>
  <div class="parenthetical">(faint, quoting his father's opera)</div>
  <div class="dialogue">"Yes, the world is a barrel organ... that the good Lord turns himself... and everyone must dance to the tune on the drum..."</div>

  <p class="action">The monitors flatline. A doctor pulls Lina backward by her shoulders.</p>

</div>

